      "local_label": "Section 1 — Covariance matrix",
      "source_kind": "definition",
      "source_heading": "Section 1 — Covariance matrix",
      "relation": "exact",
      "statement_original": "In this paper, we are interested in estimating the covariance matrix $\\Sigma=\\mathbb E[XX^\\top]$ of a random vector $X\\in\\mathbb R^d$ with zero mean from independent and identically distributed (i.i.d.) copies $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ of $X$.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "location": "Section 1 — Covariance matrix"
        }
      ],
      "highlight_symbols": [
        "\\Sigma=\\mathbb E[XX^\\top]"
      ],
      "highlight_phrases": []
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "aos-2024-v52-i05-p1953",
      "local_id": "D2",
      "local_label": "Assumption 1.2 (i.i.d. sample with contamination)",
      "source_kind": "assumption",
      "source_heading": "Assumption 1.2 (i.i.d. sample with contamination)",
      "relation": "exact",
      "statement_original": "$X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ are i.i.d. copies of a random element $X$ of $\\mathbb R^d$ satisfying $\\mathbb E[\\|X\\|^p]<+\\infty$ for some $p\\geq4$. We assume $\\mathbb E[X]=0$, that the covariance $\\Sigma$ of $X$ is non-null, and set\n\\[\n\\kappa_p:=\\sup_{v\\in\\mathbb R^d,\\,\\langle v,\\Sigma v\\rangle=1}\\mathbb E[|\\langle X,v\\rangle|^p]^{\\frac1p}.\n\\]\nFinally, we let $Y_1,\\ldots,Y_n$ denote other random elements of $\\mathbb R^d$ that satisfy the following condition:\n\\[\n\\#\\{i\\in[n]:Y_i\\ne X_i\\}\\leq\\eta n\n\\]\nfor some $\\eta\\in[0,1)$.",
      "depends_on": [
        "D1",
        "D3"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 3,
          "location": "Assumption 1.2 (i.i.d. sample with contamination)"
        }
      ],
      "highlight_symbols": [
        "\\mathbb E[\\|X\\|^p]<+\\infty",
        "\\#\\{i\\in[n]:Y_i\\ne X_i\\}\\leq\\eta n"
      ],
      "highlight_phrases": [
        "Assumption 1.2"
      ],
